title Path C: stages and the gates between them
start
:Stage 0, weeks 1 to 8: 3 to 5 interviews (W-13, W-16)
also ask: would your suppliers finance against your approved POs?; <<#D6EAF8>>
if (Gate 0: 3+ firms would pay SAR 1,500 to 7,500 a month?) then (yes)
  :Stage 1, to month 18: tender SaaS pilot, then 10 to 20 tenants
  build with a global vendor identity and signed award events; <<#AED6F1>>
  if (Gate 1: 20 paying tenants and 1,000+ vendors?) then (yes)
    :Stage 2, months 18 to 30: verified supplier profile across buyers
    (CR via Wathq, VAT, certificates); vendors still free; <<#85C1E9>>
    if (Gate 2: 30 %+ of vendors serve 2+ buyers?) then (yes)
      :Stage 3, months 24 to 36: one referral partner (Tameed, Manafa or Fina)
      legal opinion first; partner files the SAMA non-objection; <<#5DADE2>>
      if (Gate 3: SAR 50M+ financed a year, and SAR 500M+ volume visible?) then (yes)
        :**Year-3 decision**: raise and become a licensed lender (path B)
        or partner-own one; <<#58D68D>>
      else (no)
        :Stay SaaS plus referral; plan a strategic sale; <<#F8C471>>
      endif
    else (no)
      :Stay SaaS; grow tenants, not the network; <<#F8C471>>
    endif
  else (no)
    :Stop or sell to an ERP partner; <<#F5B7B1>>
  endif
else (no)
  :Stop. Lost: about 8 weeks, about SAR 0; <<#F5B7B1>>
endif
